{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And its innards and its legs he shall wash.</b> Because it comes upon the table of the king; but bulls and goats, which are burned outside — the innards and the legs do not require washing with water." "<b>He shall wash in water.</b> Washing mentioned regarding a person is translated ״יסחי״, because it is language of immersion outside, like when one spreads out to swim; but washing mentioned in the offerings is translated ״יחליל״, meaning he removes from them the waste matter and they remain hollow." "<b>He shall wash in water.</b> One might think: just as the washing mentioned below requires forty se'ah, so too the washing mentioned here should require forty se'ah — Scripture says <b>water</b> — any amount." "<b>All of it.</b> To include bones and sinews, horns and hooves, and the wool on the heads of lambs and the hair on the beards of goats, at the time they are attached."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:34.612934649Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}